Author:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
AuthorDate: Fri Feb 7 17:51:36 2025 +0000
Commit:     John Bieling <john@thunderbird.net>
CommitDate: Fri Feb 7 17:51:36 2025 +0000

    Bug 1945514 - Fix `recent` query in folders API. r=mkmelin

    When the recent query first landed, I did not know that we have two
    different "recent" properties: `MRUTime` which is updated whenever the
    folder is viewed, and `MRMTime`, which is updated whenever new messages
    are moved or copied into it.

    This patch is deprecating the original `recent` query support and
    instead adds two new query properties: `lastUsed` and `lastAdded`. Both
    are of type `QueryDateRange`, which allows to specify `recent`
    (boolean), `before` or `after` (both a Date).

    In addition, this patch adds a `sort` property, to specify how the found
    folders should be sorted, before they are returned. The former `recent`
    query automatically sorted be recentness, which was `lastUsed`. The
    query may now have the `lastUsed` and `lastAdded` property set, and it
    is no longer possible to guess by what property the folders should be
    auto-sorted.

    The deprecated `recent` query can now be achieved via

    ```
    browser.folders.query({
       lastUsed: { recent: true },
       sort: "lastUsed",
       limit: browser.folders.DEFAULT_MOST_RECENT_LIMIT
    });
    ```

    Differential Revision: https://phabricator.services.mozilla.com/D236541

